<title>USA: Alumax Inc Q2 profit.</title>
<headline>Alumax Inc Q2 profit.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second Quarter	    First Half</p>
<p>				 1997     1996	   1997	1996</p>
<p>			    (In Millions, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p> Net sales		$ 730.9  $ 851.4    $ 1,432.7 $ 1,654.0</p>
<p>Cost and expenses:</p>
<p>  Cost of goods sold    559.9    681.3	1,105.5   1,312.0</p>
<p>  Selling and general    62.4     69.8	  123.3     133.6</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>   amortization	    37.6     35.9	   74.7	68.9</p>
<p>				659.9    787.0	1,303.5   1,514.5</p>
<p>Earnings from</p>
<p> operations		  71.0     64.4	  129.2     139.5</p>
<p>Gain on sale</p>
<p>  of assets(1)		  -     92.8		-     171.2</p>
<p> Other income		 2.7	0.8	    2.4	14.9</p>
<p> Interest expense	 (13.9)   (16.9)	 (27.3)    (34.1)</p>
<p> Income taxes	     (24.0)   (58.0)	 (41.8)   (113.0)</p>
<p> Net earnings		35.8     83.1	   62.5     178.5</p>
<p> Preferred dividends	  -    (2.4)		-     (4.7)</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p> Primary			.64     1.77	   1.12	3.81</p>
<p> Fully diluted(3)	   .64     1.50	   1.12	3.23</p>
<p>Weighted average shares in millions:</p>
<p>   Primary		   55.9     45.7	   55.9	45.6</p>
<p>   Fully diluted	   56.0     55.3	   55.9	55.2</p>
<p>Pro forma earnings per share:(4)</p>
<p>   Basic			.65     1.80	   1.14	3.88</p>
<p>   Diluted		    .64     1.50	   1.12	3.23</p>
<p>(1) 1996 Q2 includes a pretax gain of $92.8 ($55.1 after tax, or $1.21 per share, $0.99 diluted) from the sale of mining investments. 1996 first half also includes a pretax gain of $78.4 ($48.6 after tax) related to the sale of a 23 percent interest in the Mt. Holly primary aluminum reduction facility.</p>
<p>(2) 1996 first half includes $18.6 ($18.3 after tax) for dividends received from investments in Mexican mining operations.</p>
<p>(3) As of December 4, 1996, substantially all of the outstanding shares of the $4.00 Series A Convertible Preferred Stock were converted into common.</p>
<p>(4) In February 1997, the Financial Accounting Standards Board issued Statement of Financial Accounting Standards No. 128, &quot;Earnings per Share&quot; (&quot;FAS 128&quot;). The Company will adopt FAS 128 in the fourth quarter of 1997. The pro forma amounts presented illustrate the Company's earnings per share as if FAS 128 had been adopted at the beginning of each period.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
